  "confidences": {"U": 0.8, "A": 0.8, "C": 0.7, "V": 0.9},
  "rationales": {
    "U": "证据'They must be able to'：主语'They'未定义，导致需求主体不明确，影响理解。",
    "A": "证据'adequate'：术语'adequate'模糊，未指定电压和频率的具体标准，导致歧义。",
    "C": "证据'self-start without any source of off-site electric power'：这可能正确，但缺乏上下文和技术细节，无法确认正确性。",
    "V": "证据'maintain adequate voltage and frequency'：未量化指标，如具体电压和频率范围，无法设计测试用例验证。"
  },
  "suggestions": {
    "U": "将'They'替换为具体设备名称，例如'The black-start capable generator'。",
    "A": "将'adequate'替换为具体数值范围，例如'voltage within ±5% of nominal and frequency within ±0.5 Hz'。",
    "C": "保持不变，但建议确认技术正确性并添加细节。",
    "V": "添加可测试的验收标准，例如'voltage maintained at 1.0 per unit ±5% and frequency at 60 Hz ±0.5 Hz'。"
  },
  "issues": [
    {"type": "U", "evidence": "They must be able to", "rewrite": "The black-start capable generator must be able to"},
    {"type": "A", "evidence": "adequate", "rewrite": "specified voltage and frequency ranges, e.g., voltage within ±5% of nominal and frequency within ±0.5 Hz"},
    {"type": "V", "evidence": "maintain adequate voltage and frequency", "rewrite": "maintain voltage at 1.0 per unit ±5% and frequency at 60 Hz ±0.5 Hz"}
  ]
}

{
  "item": "R1",
  "scores": {"U": 2, "A": 2, "C": 3, "V": 1},
  "confidences": {"U": 0.9, "A": 0.95, "C": 0.8, "V": 0.95},
  "rationales": {"U":"'They must be able to self-start without any source of off-site electric power' lacks subject identification — 'They' is ambiguous (generators? control systems? units?) and violates subject-verb clarity; also 'self-start' is colloquial and undefined in power systems context.", "A":"'without any source of off-site electric power' is ambiguous: does it exclude all external AC/DC sources including batteries, UPS, or station batteries? 'Adequate voltage and frequency' lacks numerical thresholds and tolerance bounds, making compliance judgmental.", "C":"The requirement aligns with black-start capability standards (e.g., NERC TPL-001), so technical intent is plausible; however, 'maintain adequate voltage and frequency while energizing isolated transmission facilities and auxiliary loads of other generators' conflates two distinct operational scopes — energizing transmission vs. powering auxiliaries of *other* generators — which may exceed typical black-start unit responsibility and thus risks functional overreach.", "V":"No testable criteria: 'adequate', 'maintain', 'energizing' are unquantified; no specified duration, load step, voltage/frequency tolerances (e.g., ±5% V, ±0.05 Hz), nor measurement point (PCC? generator terminals?). Absence of pass/fail thresholds makes verification impossible."},
  "suggestions": {"U":"The generator unit shall initiate black-start operation using only on-site energy storage (e.g., battery banks or flywheels) and internal control power, without connection to off-site AC or DC power sources.", "A":"The generator unit shall achieve stable synchronization within 120 seconds of initiation, maintain terminal voltage within ±5% of nominal (13.8 kV) and frequency within ±0.05 Hz of 60 Hz for ≥30 minutes while supplying the defined black-start load profile (including isolated 138-kV transmission line charging and auxiliary loads of up to two additional generator units).", "C":"The generator unit shall support black-start of the designated 138-kV transmission corridor and provide auxiliary power only to its own station service and to one adjacent generator unit’s critical auxiliaries (as listed in Appendix A); it shall not be required to energize auxiliaries of more than one other generator unit.", "V":"The generator unit shall be verified via test procedure TP-BS-01: (a) measure voltage at generator terminals under black-start load profile; (b) record deviation from 13.8 kV and 60 Hz over 30-minute continuous operation; (c) pass if RMS voltage remains 13.1–14.5 kV and frequency remains 59.95–60.05 Hz for ≥95% of duration."},
  "issues": [
    {"type":"U","evidence":"They must be able to self-start without any source of off-site electric power","rewrite":"The generator unit shall initiate black-start operation using only on-site energy storage (e.g., battery banks or flywheels) and internal control power, without connection to off-site AC or DC power sources."},
    {"type":"A","evidence":"maintain adequate voltage and frequency","rewrite":"maintain terminal voltage within ±5% of nominal (13.8 kV) and frequency within ±0.05 Hz of 60 Hz for ≥30 minutes"},
    {"type":"V","evidence":"maintain adequate voltage and frequency while energizing isolated transmission facilities and auxiliary loads of other generators","rewrite":"The generator unit shall be verified via test procedure TP-BS-01: (a) measure voltage at generator terminals under black-start load profile; (b) record deviation from 13.8 kV and 60 Hz over 30-minute continuous operation; (c) pass if RMS voltage remains 13.1–14.5 kV and frequency remains 59.95–60.05 Hz for ≥95% of duration."}
  ]
}
